<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to allow bank ADRs in Annex Four portfolios.</title>
<headline>Brazil to allow bank ADRs in Annex Four portfolios.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors will be allowed to include American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) issued by Brazilian banks in their locally held investment portfolios known as Annex Four, a Central Bank director said.</p>
<p>The change was included in norms approved by the National Monetary Council Thursday that will govern the issuing by Brazilian banks of ADRs.</p>
<p>A decree signed earlier this month by President Fernando Henrique Cardoso allows banks to sell ADRs, convertible in non-voting shares only, in an attempt to bring more capital into Brazil's financial sector.</p>
<p>Central Bank Norms Director Alkimar Moura said the move to allow foreigners to hold bank ADRs in their Annex Four portfolios would further encourage investment in the sector.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
